# infra-os:   alpine
# infra-init: openrc
# infra-path: /etc/snapper
# infra-name: snapper
# infra-mode: 0644
#
# snapper's list of configs, which only the package's own scripts read: Alpine's snapper
# puts here what openSUSE keeps in /etc/sysconfig/snapper. It is empty, as the package
# ships it, and tracked so it stays empty. /etc/periodic/hourly/snapper, the package's
# hourly script, runs snapper for each config named here without --no-dbus, so it would
# need the D-Bus daemon, which zero does not run. Empty, it does nothing; snapper-immich
# takes zero's snapshots instead (plans/three-backup-pull.md).
#
# At zero's move to Leap, `immich` is added to Leap's /etc/sysconfig/snapper, and Leap's
# own timers take over.

SNAPPER_CONFIGS=""
